# Environment Variables

## Required

| Variable | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `KV_URL` | Vercel KV connection string (provisioned via `vercel env add KV_URL production`) | `redis://default:***@redis-12345.0.ngrok-free.app:6379` |
| `KV_REST_API_URL` | Vercel KV REST API URL | `https://your-kv.vercel-storage.com` |
| `KV_REST_API_TOKEN` | Vercel KV REST API token | `eyJhbGciOi...` |

> **Note:** All three KV variables are automatically set when you run `vercel env add .env.local` after provisioning KV through the Vercel dashboard. The `@vercel/kv` package uses these three.

## Optional

| Variable | Description | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `MANGA_DEX_USER_AGENT` | User-Agent string sent to MangaDex | `OtakuReader/1.0.0 (...)` | Must be set per MangaDex API TOS; do NOT use `Via` header |
| `MANGA_DEX_BASE_URL` | Override MangaDex API base | `https://api.mangadex.org` | Only needed for testing against staging |
| `ANILIST_RATE_LIMIT_TOKENS` | AniList token bucket capacity | `30` | Reduced from 90 due to current degradation |
| `NODE_ENV` | Runtime environment | `production` | Standard Node.js env var |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Structured log level | `info` | `debug` for dev, `warn` for prod |
| `CORS_ORIGIN` | Allowed CORS origin(s) | `*` | Comma-separated list; set to your domain(s) in production |

## Rate Limit Environment Variables

These are read at startup and can be tuned without redeploy:

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `RATE_LIMIT_MANGA_DEX_TOKENS` | `5` | Global token bucket capacity |
| `RATE_LIMIT_MANGA_DEX_REFILL_MS` | `1000` | Refill period (1 token per second) |
| `RATE_LIMIT_AT_HOME_TOKENS` | `40` | At-home chapter image bucket |
| `RATE_LIMIT_AT_HOME_REFILL_MS` | `60000` | 40 tokens per minute |
| `RATE_LIMIT_ANILIST_TOKENS` | `30` | AniList token bucket (degraded from 90) |
| `RATE_LIMIT_JIKAN_TOKENS` | `3` | Jikan token bucket |
| `RATE_LIMIT_JIKAN_REFILL_MS` | `1000` | Jikan refill period |

## Content Filtering (runtime-toggleable, no env var needed)

Content ratings are hardcoded to `['safe', 'suggestive']` per MVP spec. To allow `safe` only, change `ALLOWED_CONTENT_RATINGS` in `src/lib/api/constants.ts`.

## Vercel KV Provisioning

```bash
# Install Vercel KV (Redis)
vercel env add KV_URL production    # prompted for Redis URL
vercel env add KV_REST_API_URL production
vercel env add KV_REST_API_TOKEN production

# Or use Vercel Dashboard: Storage → Create Database → KV
# Then link with:
vercel link
vercel env pull
```

## CORS Origins (if restricting later)

Currently set to `*` via `CORS_ORIGIN`. To lock down:

```env
CORS_ORIGIN=https://otakureader.app,https://www.otakureader.app
```

## Logging

Logs go to Vercel's native log drain (structured JSON by default in Node.js 20.x runtime). Use `LOG_LEVEL=debug` locally.
